# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{index.html}
= jemdocx -- modern jemdoc for Python 3

jemdocx is a maintained fork of [https://github.com/jem/jemdoc jemdoc], the
lightweight markup language created by Jacob Mattingley in 2007. The original
+0.7.3+ release targets Python 2; this fork preserves its concise syntax while
supporting current Python 3 versions, UTF-8 content, automated testing, and a
modern equation-rendering path.

The generator remains deliberately small. A jemdoc source file, an optional
menu and configuration, and a CSS file are enough to build a clean static site.

== Current highlights
- Python 3.8 and newer; no third-party Python packages.
- UTF-8 source and output files.
- [latex.html MathJax 4 equations] by default, without a local TeX install.
- Optional legacy +latex+ and +dvipng+ PNG rendering.
- Compatibility with classic jemdoc markup, menus, configuration, and themes.
- Regression tests across multiple Python 3 releases.

== Getting started
Run the generator from the repository root:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc index.jemdoc
~~~

Windows users can use +py -3+ in place of +python3+. Continue with the
[using.html usage guide], browse the [example.html example], or keep the
[cheatsheet.html cheat sheet] nearby while writing.

== Project direction
This fork is a conservative modernization rather than a redesign. Its priorities
are compatibility, Unicode correctness, maintainable Python, reproducible
builds, and clean web output. Historical release snapshots are available from
the upstream Git history instead of being duplicated here.

